      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(auto-reply): degrade gracefully when preflight compaction hard-fails",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses #100778 — a preflight compaction LLM failure (timeout, rate limit, provider 5xx) aborted the whole reply and left the Control UI/webchat Composer permanently in a \"terminated\" state; the user could not send another message without a page refresh.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`runPreflightCompactionIfNeeded` threw on a non-`ok` compaction result. The throw propagated to the chat dispatch-error lifecycle, which cleared the chat run and left the Composer \"killed\". The code itself documents the intent that preflight compaction is a guardrail, not a hard dependency.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner-memory.ts`: both failure throw sites in `runPreflightCompactionIfNeeded` now skip compaction and return the session entry (continuing the agent run) instead of throwing. The failure is still logged via `logVerbose`.\n- Benign skip reasons (`below_threshold`, `no_compactable_entries`, `already_compacted_recently`) are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest run --pool forks src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner-memory.preflight-stale-tokens.test.ts` — 3 passed (incl. new regression test asserting a hard compaction failure resolves without throwing and returns the entry).\n- `oxlint` clean (0/0), `oxfmt --check` clean on the changed file.\n\n## Note\n\nThis makes the failure path non-fatal (degrade by skipping compaction), matching the documented \"guardrail, not a hard dependency\" intent. If maintainers prefer a different recovery (e.g. surfacing an actionable error toast while keeping the Composer enabled), that can layer on top of this change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "branch": "fix/preflight-compaction-graceful",
